    "content": "All 18 checklist items have been executed and recorded: **12 PASS, 6 FAIL**.\n\nThe core in-session forum flows work well — registration with duplicate/password validation, profile editing, thread creation with field validation, live replies, upvote toggling, case-insensitive search, category filtering, and both Trending (by upvotes) and Most Active (by replies) re-ranking correctly when activity changes.\n\nThe six failures cluster into four real defects:\n\n- **CS-17 — Authentication is not enforced.** Sign-in accepts *any* password for a registered email, granting a full session. This is the most severe finding.\n- **FT-18 — Nothing persists.** A page reload wipes the session, registered accounts, profile edits, threads, replies and votes; `localStorage` is empty and state resets to seed data. (FT-13 passed because logout/login within one loaded page keeps in-memory state.)\n- **CS-22 — Blank page instead of a sign-in gate.** A logged-out user reaching discussion creation gets an entirely empty render, with no redirect, message, or way back to creating a thread — and the logged-out UI offers no entry point at all.\n- **CT-19 / CT-20 / CT-21 — Fabricated numbers.** Seeded threads carry inflated counters unrelated to reality: thread-4 claims 68 replies but lists 2; Community Stats claim 1,045 threads / 4,823 replies / 892 members against 10 actual threads, and never move when records are created; and the \"trending/most active\" views state no recent time window, ranking purely on all-time totals so 2-year-old threads dominate while today's activity ranks last."
